DECISION CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge
	TITLE "every mechanical step of a wave is a CLI command; a model is called only to judge"
	STATUS active
	DESC "branches, worktrees, ordering, launching, polling, merging, rebasing, statistics, report"
		+ "skeletons and signal normalisation are deterministic code of the CLI; an agent receives"
		+ "a pre-computed context from one command and returns a verdict or a text through another"
	REJECTED "a coordinator agent that orchestrates the wave: it rediscovers state at every step"
		+ "and spends judgment on bookkeeping"
	REJECTED "letting each run read git, gh and files itself: measured, the first edit of a task"
		+ "run came after 23 steps and 134 000 tokens in median"
	RATIONALE "the user's first principle for the plan; the measured cost of discovery is the"
		+ "largest saving available"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 1 and 5"

DECISION TheToolIsNamedBrigade
	TITLE "the CLI, the repository and the config directory are named brigade"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the kitchen brigade is the team of roles under the chef, who is the user; the"
		+ "verification gate is nicknamed the pass"
	REJECTED "fab: collides with the Fabric CLI"
	REJECTED "chef, kitchen: collide with the Chef ecosystem's CLIs"
	REJECTED "expo, pass: collide with the Expo CLI and the pass password store"
	RATIONALE "free on PATH and in Debian packages on 2026-10-04; the metaphor is the one the user"
		+ "adopted from the talk"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 3"

DECISION PythonStandardLibraryOnly
	TITLE "brigade is Python 3.11 or later, standard library only, with POSIX sh only in the"
		+ "optional scheduler files; no third-party dependency"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "a Bun or TypeScript CLI: ties a machine-wide tool to a JavaScript toolchain the"
		+ "instructions corpus does not have"
	REJECTED "a TUI framework: a new dependency for views the web dashboard renders"
	RATIONALE "the hooks, the unattended runner and the user's local context page are already"
		+ "Python and sh; 3.11 is the floor tomllib needs and nothing in the plan needs a later"
		+ "feature"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 15 and 16"

DECISION ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent
	TITLE "the coordinator is brigade tick, a deterministic pass run every five minutes by the"
		+ "machine's scheduler: the user systemd timer where a user instance runs, else a cron line"
		+ "or brigade tick --loop"
	STATUS active
	DESC "it reconciles waves with git and GitHub, advances task states, launches runs within the"
		+ "slot cap, merges verified pull requests and records events"
	REJECTED "a long-lived coordinator session: costs tokens for waiting and loses state at"
		+ "compaction"
	REJECTED "cloud routines: private data and the worktrees are on the machine only"
	RATIONALE "every transition is a condition evaluated from facts; the laptop being off loses"
		+ "nothing, the next tick after boot resumes"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 5 and 17"

DECISION HybridStorageCorpusAndLedger
	TITLE "durable facts live in awawa corpora, high-volume events in an append-only JSONL ledger"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the brigade corpus holds PROJECT, POLICY, STUDY, ORDER, REQUEST, PATTERN and CONSTRAINT;"
		+ "each project corpus keeps its WAVE and TASK entities; the ledger holds runs, states,"
		+ "pauses and merges"
	REJECTED "everything in awawa: one entity per run means thousands of entities and git noise"
	REJECTED "SQLite for everything: a second grammar without schema lint"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer to the storage question; one home per fact, views rendered never"
		+ "hand-maintained"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 13 and 14"

DECISION AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
	TITLE "every pull request passes a deterministic preflight then one prudence run before merging"
		+ "into integration; the user merges integration into main"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "the user reviewing every diff: the rung the user asked to leave"
	REJECTED "sampling that blocks: sampling stays a suggestion in the report"
	RATIONALE "the user's answers on autonomy and review; delivered work is never verified by the"
		+ "run that produced it"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 7"

DECISION QuotaPausesTheWaveAndResumesTheSameSession
	TITLE "a rate-limit result pauses the wave; the resume is the adapter's resume of the suspended"
		+ "session at the time the message names, or a fresh launch from the progress file when the"
		+ "adapter has no resume"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "a dollar cap: the subscription is the cap"
	REJECTED "probing the quota with extra calls: the resume itself is the probe"
	REJECTED "treating a client without resume as unsupported: the progress file is the contract"
		+ "every run already keeps"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer on budget: waves of 10 to 20 pull requests, the quota blocks"
		+ "before any overspend"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 17"

DECISION TheDashboardIsBuiltThePluginAndAwawaWebAreKept
	TITLE "a loopback web dashboard is built; the IntelliJ plugin stays for in-IDE work; awawa-web"
		+ "stays the editor of the brigade corpus"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the dashboard exposes a local JSON API the plugin may consume later for a branch selector"
	REJECTED "extending the plugin into the factory's UI: it would have to grow a server and a"
		+ "ledger reader of its own"
	REJECTED "a second corpus editor in the dashboard: awawa-web already edits block by block with"
		+ "fmt and lint"
	RATIONALE "the plugin's handbook names user-defined views as its extension point; the branch"
		+ "selector is a server-side fact (git archive per SHA)"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 15"

DECISION AwawaIsWrappedAsItIs
	TITLE "the plan wraps the awawa binary as it is; desired changes go to a list of requests to"
		+ "its author, never on the critical path"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "forking awawa or waiting for a feature: the user is a consumer and the author may"
		+ "lack time"
	RATIONALE "every awawa gap has a workaround the POC uses: block edits with fmt and lint,"
		+ "per-entity spawns cached per SHA"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 19"

DECISION MinedConstraintsAreDeliveredAsWaves
	TITLE "constraints mined from transcripts become waves like any other work, auto-merged into"
		+ "integration and listed in the report with their reason"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the scrubber runs inside the transcript collectors before anything is written, on the"
		+ "PRIVATE patterns of each registered project and on brigade's built-ins, e-mail addresses"
		+ "and home paths; a set computed at run time is never stored"
	REJECTED "proposals only in the dashboard: the user asked for the same autonomy as a wave"
	REJECTED "a stored list of real names for the scrubber: no correspondence between a real name"
		+ "and a pseudonym is kept anywhere"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer on mining; no real identifier leaves the machine"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 12"

DECISION TheCorpusIsTheHomeOfTaskStatusTheBoardItsView
	TITLE "the corpus is the single home of task status; the task board of the Artifact is a view"
		+ "of it"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a task's STATUS is edited in corpus/tasks.awawa and nowhere else"
	DESC "the board of the Blueprint shows the status the corpus holds, written by a deterministic"
		+ "command"
	DESC "a status changed on the board binds nothing"
	REJECTED "the board as the home of status until the brigade delivers its own waves, the"
		+ "planning run's choice: the corpus held every task draft while the board showed them"
		+ "todo, two homes already disagreeing"
	REJECTED "two homes kept in sync by hand: a hand-maintained view is wrong by the next commit"
	RATIONALE "the plan's own principle, one home per fact, views rendered never hand-maintained;"
		+ "ruled by the user on 2026-10-05"
	SOURCE "pull request #1 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	TITLE "brigade's core names no AI client: every launch, result, resume, transcript read and"
		+ "tool grant goes through a client adapter, and each capability a client lacks has a"
		+ "recorded fallback"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a client adapter answers six operations as JSON documents, probe, launch, result, resume,"
		+ "transcripts and actions; it is a built-in module or an executable brigade-client-<name>"
		+ "on PATH"
	DESC "probe declares the optional operations the client supports; the core applies the fallback"
		+ "of each missing one: no resume, a fresh launch from the progress file; no step count,"
		+ "steps null and the budget held on wall time; no transcripts, brigade's journal of the"
		+ "run; no actions, one raw record per line of the client's output; no per-tool grant, the"
		+ "client's unattended mode and a disposable worktree for a reading slot; no reset hour in"
		+ "a rate-limit message, now plus thirty minutes"
	DESC "the core spawns the process itself, in the worktree, with the brief, the role package,"
		+ "the capabilities and the budget the adapter translated; the ledger wraps every client"
		+ "the same way"
	DESC "worktrees are git's, never the client's; background sessions of a client are not used"
	DESC "the README lists the supported clients and, for each adapter operation, the support"
		+ "level, full, fallback or absent, generated from the probe declarations; a test fails"
		+ "when the table drifts"
	DESC "the Claude Code adapter is the first; the sandbox rehearsal runs on every installed"
		+ "adapter and on the fake adapter the test suite launches"
	REJECTED "brigade as hooks, commands and agent files of one CLI: unusable with another client,"
		+ "and the instructions corpus already rules its own files agent-agnostic"
	REJECTED "an SDK per client: a third-party dependency each, where the command line of a client"
		+ "is the contract its vendor documents"
	REJECTED "refusing a client that lacks resume or per-tool grants: each fallback above costs"
		+ "nothing a wave cannot absorb"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-05 that brigade presupposes neither Claude Code nor its"
		+ "workings and that the README names the supported tools with their level; four clients"
		+ "document a non-interactive mode with a JSON output (Claude Code 2.1.289 --help, Codex"
		+ "exec, OpenCode run, Gemini headless, read on 2026-10-05) and only Claude Code is"
		+ "installed on the reference machine"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION RolesAreSlotsBoundToRoleFiles
	TITLE "a procedure calls a slot, never a role name; a role is a Markdown file with a flat front"
		+ "matter and a system prompt body; a slot resolves to a role in a fixed order ending on"
		+ "brigade's built-in roles"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the slots are plan, build, verify, review, rebase, report, triage, rules and explore"
	DESC "a role file declares name, slot, reasoning (deepest, deep, standard, light), capabilities"
		+ "(read, write, shell, net), budget and returns; its body is the whole system prompt of"
		+ "the run"
	DESC "a slot resolves in this order: a PROJECT.ROLE override, the machine's roles directory,"
		+ "the AGENT entities of the instructions corpus when config names one, brigade's built-in"
		+ "roles"
	DESC "an AGENT entity is read through awawa --json at launch time: WORK, REASONING, CAPABILITY,"
		+ "BUDGET and RETURNS fill the front matter, its context package is the body"
	DESC "the reasoning level maps to a model and an effort in the client adapter's table,"
		+ "overridable in the machine config; a role file never names a model"
	DESC "brigade ships a built-in role for every slot, named after its work: planner, builder,"
		+ "verifier, reviewer, rebaser, reporter, triager, rulewriter and explorer"
	DESC "an AGENT entity declares no slot: it takes the slot a table of config.toml written by its"
		+ "user binds it to; brigade ships no binding and no name of its author's agents"
	REJECTED "roles living only in the instructions corpus: presupposes that corpus on every"
		+ "machine"
	REJECTED "roles written in one client's agent-file format: bound to that client"
	REJECTED "a model name in a role file: the depth is the role's and the model the adapter's, as"
		+ "the AGENT schema of the instructions corpus already states"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for custom roles and for their own roles by default;"
		+ "@SCHEMA.AGENT of the instructions corpus separates REASONING from the model each adapter"
		+ "binds"
	REJECTED "built-in roles named after the agents of the author's instructions corpus, replaced"
		+ "by name: brigade would ship its author's machine"
	REJECTED "built-in roles with a person's name, ada, bilal and mina: the names of the author's"
		+ "own agents, which say nothing of the work a slot does"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "DESC 7 added on the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 in the refinement of B43"
	SOURCE "DESC 6 and the last REJECTED: the review of pull request #20 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites
	TITLE "brigade installs on any Linux from one zipapp or a clone; Python 3.11 or later, git,"
		+ "awawa and one adapted AI client are the prerequisites; the scheduler, the forge account,"
		+ "the instructions corpus and the IDE tools are optional"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade doctor checks Python 3.11 or later, git, awawa 2.7 or later and the configured"
		+ "client adapter's probe, and reports each optional item with its fallback as a warning,"
		+ "never a finding"
	DESC "optional with its fallback: a user systemd instance, else a cron line or brigade tick"
		+ "--loop; gh with the machine account, else the user's gh account recorded in the ledger"
		+ "on every write, else local mode without a forge; the instructions corpus, else built-in"
		+ "roles and no instructions package; awawa-web and the IDE plugin, dashboard only"
	DESC "machine bindings live in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/config.toml: client, scheduler, forge"
		+ "account, instructions corpus root, the reasoning-to-model table, the IDE link; ratified"
		+ "facts stay in the corpus"
	DESC "custom roles, collectors, checks and recipes live under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/ in"
		+ "roles/, collectors/, checks/ and recipes/; state in $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/; the refs"
		+ "and collector caches in $XDG_CACHE_HOME/brigade/"
	DESC "the repository builds dist/brigade.pyz with the standard zipapp module; the file runs"
		+ "with python3 alone"
	REJECTED "pip or pipx: absent from the reference Debian 13 (command -v pip pipx, 2026-10-05)"
	REJECTED "systemd as a prerequisite: the tick is one command any scheduler runs"
	REJECTED "machine bindings as corpus entities: a probed capability is not a ratified fact, and"
		+ "the corpus is a git history"
	REJECTED "awawa optional, the progress of a run falling back to Markdown without it: a refactor"
		+ "of the registry, the policies and every corpus read for nothing, brigade reading no"
		+ "project of projects.awawa without awawa"
	REJECTED "awawa embedded in the brigade binary: awawa is a native ELF x86-64 binary and brigade"
		+ "a stdlib-only zipapp that runs with python3 alone, so one binary per architecture would"
		+ "be extracted to disk at run time, against DESC 5"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-05 that brigade installs and runs on another Linux machine"
		+ "with another AI client"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's word of 2026-10-07, \"ok\", at the drafting of @TASK.B106, pull request #64"
		+ "of the brigade repository, on the proposal \"Je recommande A. … Concrètement : la clé"
		+ "`document` de `config.toml` vaut `awawa` par défaut ; `markdown` reste disponible par"
		+ "configuration ; `brigade doctor` continue de signaler l'absence d'awawa comme un"
		+ "problème.\""
		REF @TASK.B106

DECISION ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles
	TITLE "the command line with --json is the contract, state lives in language-neutral files and"
		+ "black-box CLI tests are the acceptance suite, so that a port to another language is a"
		+ "port and not a redesign"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every command prints --json with stable field names and the documented exit codes; the"
		+ "dashboard and the agents use the command line, never the package; tests/cli is the"
		+ "acceptance suite a port must pass; tests/unit and tests/integration test the Python and"
		+ "die with it"
	DESC "state is JSONL, JSON, TOML, Markdown with a flat front matter and awawa corpora; recipes"
		+ "are TOML; no pickle, shelve or private database; a sqlite file may only be a derived"
		+ "cache deletable at any time"
	DESC "every result, event, collector, recipe and config document carries a schema version"
	DESC "tests/cli drives brigade as a subprocess against fixtures, a sandbox git repository, the"
		+ "fake client adapter and recorded forge answers; a port passes this suite before"
		+ "replacing the Python"
	DESC "the client, forge and scheduler adapters, the collectors, the checks and the outputs are"
		+ "process-shaped boundaries: a built-in one is a module, an external one an executable on"
		+ "PATH, both answering the same JSON documents"
	DESC "the core never imports an adapter module; a guard script under tests checks the import"
		+ "graph"
	DESC "the language of the distributed version is decided at M3 with the ledger's measures, Go"
		+ "or Rust"
	REJECTED "a Rust rewrite now: no toolchain on the reference machine (command -v rustc cargo,"
		+ "2026-10-05), every crate a dependency the standard-library ruling refuses, and the"
		+ "tool's shape still open"
	REJECTED "a Go rewrite now: the same absent toolchain; Go stays the target that keeps a"
		+ "standard-library-only policy with a static binary"
	REJECTED "PyInstaller or Nuitka: third-party packagers for what zipapp does"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for an architecture that eases a later migration to"
		+ "Rust or another distributable form; what these rules keep outside the Python package is"
		+ "what a port carries over unchanged"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "DESC 1 amended on the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade"
		+ "repository"

DECISION AStudyIsDeterministicCollectorsThenOneJudgingRun
	TITLE "work that is not a wave, a report, a data collection, an audit, a research, is a study:"
		+ "declared deterministic collectors assemble the evidence, then at most one judging run"
		+ "answers from that evidence alone and returns through brigade study answer"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a STUDY entity of the brigade corpus holds the question verbatim, the project when there"
		+ "is one, the collectors, the judging slot or none, the schedule or none, the output and"
		+ "an optional template"
	DESC "a collector is a declared executable or built-in that prints one JSON document, run by"
		+ "the CLI with the study's parameters in its environment, cached by the hash of its"
		+ "command and inputs, never a model"
	DESC "collectors resolve in order: the project's .brigade/collectors/, the machine's collectors"
		+ "directory, brigade-collector-<name> on PATH, brigade's built-ins; the shell collector"
		+ "runs a command line declared in the study"
	DESC "brigade study context prints the question, each collector's summary with the path of its"
		+ "full document, the template's skeleton filled with the collected values and the expected"
		+ "shape of the answer; the judging run reads nothing a collector already collected"
	DESC "brigade study answer validates the answer, refuses one that changed a CLI-filled section"
		+ "of the skeleton, writes it to the declared output, inbox signal, file on a branch,"
		+ "corpus entity or forge issue, and records the ledger event; an executable"
		+ "brigade-output-<name> on PATH adds an output"
	DESC "the report slot answers with a narrative, the explore slot with findings and their"
		+ "evidence, the triage slot with patterns, the rules slot with rules"
	DESC "a study with no judging slot is a scan: its non-empty output is the answer; the gardening"
		+ "scans of M4 declare OUTPUT inbox"
	DESC "the wave report, the triage and the miner are the built-in studies wave-report, triage"
		+ "and mine-transcripts"
	DESC "a study runs on demand with brigade study run, or when due, by the tick, under the slot"
		+ "cap; a study that needs a second judgment is two studies, the second reading the first's"
		+ "answer through the study collector"
	DESC "study is the built-in recipe study, its ordered steps collect, judge and output written"
		+ "under the recipe engine's contract; its collect steps come from the STUDY entity's"
		+ "COLLECTOR lines"
	REJECTED "a judging run that collects by itself: the two explorer runs the user saw spent"
		+ "judgment on collection, the measured cost of discovery"
	REJECTED "one entity per kind, routine, report, triage, miner: four schedulers, four context"
		+ "builders and four answer writers for one shape"
	REJECTED "collectors as Python modules only: a port would carry them, where an executable"
		+ "printing JSON is the same contract in any language"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 whether brigade separates judgment from mechanics for"
		+ "work that is not a wave; the first principle applies to every kind of work, and the"
		+ "miner of the plan already had this shape for one case"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION AKindOfWorkIsARecipeAnInstanceAnOrder
	TITLE "a user declares a new kind of work as a recipe, a TOML file of ordered process-shaped"
		+ "steps run by one engine of the tick; an order is one instance of a recipe; wave stays"
		+ "native and study is the first built-in recipe"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a recipe declares schema, name, description, params, max_wall and ordered steps of the"
		+ "kinds collect, command, gate, judge, output, order, corpus and op, op being worktree,"
		+ "commit, pull-request or merge through the adapters; a value substitutes {param} from the"
		+ "order and the project, nothing else: no expression, no loop, no fan-out"
	DESC "a judge step names a slot, a procedure and the shape of its answer; it receives only the"
		+ "run directory's documents through brigade order context, answers through brigade order"
		+ "answer, and is a run with its procedure's budget, counted in the slot cap and recorded"
		+ "in the ledger"
	DESC "a gate step names a check, an executable printing ok and reason, resolved like a"
		+ "collector; a failed gate or command parks the order with the step's reason unless the"
		+ "recipe says skip, stop or retry:N; nothing is assumed, and a parked order resumes once"
		+ "the user acted"
	DESC "each step's result is a file under the run directory; a resumed order restarts at its"
		+ "first undone step; the ledger holds order.started, step.done, step.failed, order.parked"
		+ "and order.done"
	DESC "recipes resolve in order: the project's .brigade/recipes/, the machine's recipes"
		+ "directory, brigade's built-in recipes in a data/ folder under brigade/; brigade recipe"
		+ "lint checks the schema, that every collector, check, output, procedure and slot"
		+ "resolves, that every param is declared, and refuses a client or model key"
		REF @DECISION.ShippedFilesLiveInsideThePackageAndAreReadAsResources
	DESC "an ORDER entity of the brigade corpus holds the recipe, the project, the user's words,"
		+ "the parameters, the schedule and the output; a REQUEST is the order of the native recipe"
		+ "wave, a STUDY the order of the recipe study; a recipe places a wave or another order"
		+ "through an order step"
	DESC "the engine arrives in M8, once wave and study exist: study is written in M1 as ordered"
		+ "steps under the engine's contract, so the engine replaces its orchestration without a"
		+ "command changing"
	REJECTED "a workflow language with expressions, loops and fan-out: a second language to lint,"
		+ "and the wave's scheduling, the one lifecycle that needs loops and fan-out, is exact code"
		+ "whose savings the plan measures"
	REJECTED "the wave as a declared recipe: fan-out per task, repair loops with caps, the overlap"
		+ "order and the quota pause are code; a recipe places a wave order instead"
	REJECTED "recipes as corpus entities: a recipe is nested and code-like, versioned with the"
		+ "project it serves; the corpus keeps the orders, which are facts"
	REJECTED "the engine in M1: until a second recipe exists it would generalise one case; the"
		+ "contract is fixed in M1 and the engine built in M8"
	REJECTED "the names workflow, playbook, procedure and routine: the first is the vocabulary of"
		+ "the continuous integration the pass reads check runs from, the second another tool's"
		+ "term outside the kitchen, the third the portable file a judging step runs, the fourth"
		+ "the name just merged into study"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for a way to add kinds of work on demand and proposed"
		+ "the word recipe; the user's own usage-report command, 21 000 characters bound to one"
		+ "client, is the first recipe to write: three collectors, one gate, one judging run, one"
		+ "file on the pull request's branch"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "DESC 5 amended on the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade"
		+ "repository"

DECISION TheBlueprintIsADevelopmentArtefactRetiredByTheDashboard
	TITLE "the Blueprint Artifact is an artefact of brigade's development phase, retired when the"
		+ "dashboard shows the corpus's tasks"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the Blueprint Artifact, plan, mockups, demo and task board, lives for the development of"
		+ "brigade and no longer"
	DESC "it is retired when the Corpus view of the dashboard (M3) shows every task of the brigade"
		+ "corpus with its status; the board is then republished no more"
	DESC "until then the board is a view of corpus/tasks.awawa, refreshed from awawa status TASK at"
		+ "each republication of the Artifact, never by hand"
	DESC "at retirement the plan is frozen as a dated document, readable, never rewritten; a SOURCE"
		+ "naming a section of the plan reads the frozen plan"
	DESC "the board page carries no automated test; it is checked by viewing the published page"
	REJECTED "regular-expression tests of the page source, the tests of pull request #5: they test"
		+ "how the code is written, not what the page shows, for a page that will be retired"
	REJECTED "a JavaScript test runtime for the page: a runtime adopted for a page that will be"
		+ "retired"
	REJECTED "a sync command of brigade writing the corpus's statuses to the board, B41 of pull"
		+ "request #4: a command written for a page that will be retired, when a republication"
		+ "refreshes the view"
	REJECTED "deleting the plan at retirement: the decisions cite its sections as SOURCE"
	RATIONALE "ruled by the user on 2026-10-05: the Blueprint has no life beyond the implementation"
		+ "of brigade, its board is superseded by the dashboard brigade serves itself, and its plan"
		+ "becomes a dated document once brigade exists; the same day the tests of the board page"
		+ "were ruled to test the wrong thing, the page being proven by looking at it"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #6 of the brigade repository"

DECISION TheCorpusFolderIsDeclaredByTheProjectAndDefaultsToCorpus
	TITLE "a project's corpus lives in the folder its PROJECT entity declares, corpus/ by default"
		+ "when brigade creates it; this repository's own corpus is corpus/"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the folder of a project's corpus is the CORPUS field of its PROJECT entity, relative to"
		+ "the project's path"
	DESC "a corpus brigade creates for a project (project add --init-corpus) goes in corpus/ unless"
		+ "the user names another folder"
	DESC "an existing corpus is registered where awawa finds it: project add discovers the root and"
		+ "writes CORPUS"
	DESC "the wave reports go in waves/ under that corpus folder"
	DESC "the corpus of the brigade repository is corpus/: _schema.awawa, project.awawa,"
		+ "milestones.awawa, tasks.awawa, decisions.awawa"
	REJECTED "docs/ as the fixed place of every corpus and docs/waves/ of its wave reports, the"
		+ "planning run's choice: the user refused docs/ for this repository and ruled the place"
		+ "configurable"
	REJECTED "one folder imposed on every managed project, whatever its name: a project declares"
		+ "where its specification lives"
	RATIONALE "ruled by the user on 2026-10-05: docs/ did not suit them for the specification of"
		+ "this repository, corpus/ is the name they gave it, brigade's convention for the projects"
		+ "it manages is configurable, and its default is the same as this repository"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #7 of the brigade repository"

DECISION TheCodeIsOneFlatPackageWhoseSubpackagesFollowTheComponents
	TITLE "brigade is one flat package at the repository root, a subpackage per component created"
		+ "by the first task of that component, one public function per module, four test suites"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade/ at the repository root, run by bin/brigade or dist/brigade.pyz; no src/ layout,"
		+ "no setup.py, no pyproject, no pip install"
	DESC "a subpackage of brigade/ per COMPONENT of the tasks (ledger, registry, corpus, runs,"
		+ "tick, waves, verify for the pass, studies, intake, recipes, dashboard, roles), created"
		+ "by the first task of that component, never ahead of it"
	DESC "brigade/commands/ one module per command line and nothing else, its renderers, request"
		+ "reader and exit decision underscored in it; brigade/command.py the record type every"
		+ "command module declares; brigade/cli.py discovers the command modules, builds the parser"
		+ "from their records through brigade/add_command_parsers.py and keeps the exit mapping;"
		+ "brigade/launcher.py the floor check; brigade/adapters/clients, forges and schedulers,"
		+ "brigade/collectors/, brigade/checks/ and brigade/outputs/ the plugins; brigade/system/"
		+ "the primitives: paths, clock, processes, locks, atomic files, ids, documents;"
		+ "brigade/git/ the git gateway, as brigade/corpus/ is the awawa one"
		REF @DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa
	DESC "a module exposes one public function named after a verb, no leading underscore, its"
		+ "helpers underscored, with the constants and frozen dataclasses it declares; its unit"
		+ "test is tests/unit/<same path>/test_<module>.py, as brigade/python_floor.py and"
		+ "tests/unit/test_python_floor.py of @TASK.B01 do"
		REF @TASK.B01
	DESC "launcher.py and python_floor.py run before the floor check: they use no syntax or"
		+ "annotation newer than the interpreters they refuse; the CI floor job proves 3.10 only"
	DESC "tests/cli is the acceptance suite, through the entry points as subprocesses;"
		+ "tests/integration the gateways, against a real git repository or awawa corpus in a"
		+ "temporary directory; tests/unit the pure functions; tests/guards the import graph, the"
		+ "environment reads and the README table"
	DESC "public functions, dataclasses and plugin operations carry type annotations read by the"
		+ "IDE; every parameter named runtime, private functions included, is annotated runtime:"
		+ "Runtime, which the guard tests/guards/find_unannotated_runtimes.py proves; no checker"
		+ "runs in CI; adopting one is a tool introduction discussed with the user"
	DESC "binds every code task from @TASK.B02; @TASK.B42 writes the guards, @TASK.B21 the"
		+ "integration fixtures"
		REF @TASK.B02
		REF @TASK.B42
		REF @TASK.B21
	REJECTED "src/brigade/: an install layout for a package nobody pip-installs; it only lengthens"
		+ "the path bin/brigade inserts"
	REJECTED "the component directories created now, empty: an empty package reads as architecture"
		+ "and is not; each arrives with its task"
	REJECTED "one module per component: the one-exported-function rule of the instructions corpus"
		+ "and the IMPL anchors need module names that say what they hold"
	REJECTED "mypy or pyright in CI now: a third-party tool nobody asked for; the IDE on the"
		+ "reference machine checks the annotations live"
	REJECTED "a render_*.py or helper module beside the command modules: commands/ then holds two"
		+ "kinds of modules and cannot be discovered as the list of commands"
	REJECTED "one command module declaring several command lines: the lines it serves are found by"
		+ "reading it, not by listing commands/"
	REJECTED "a hand-written list of the command modules in cli.py: one more place to touch per"
		+ "command, which discovery makes useless once commands/ holds commands alone"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for strict foundations before the code of M0 grows; the"
		+ "layout applies the rules one_exported_function_per_file, yagni, kiss, test_scope_levels"
		+ "and tool_introduction_is_the_users_call of the instructions corpus"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "DESC 3 amended on the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 in the refinement of @TASK.B82, F26"
		+ "and F27 of the foundations review"
		REF @TASK.B82
	REJECTED "the parser builder private to brigade/cli.py: its refusals of a path declared twice"
		+ "and of two helps for one group could then be unit-tested only through an underscored"
		+ "name"
	SOURCE "brigade/add_command_parsers.py named in DESC 3 in pull request #56 of the brigade"
		+ "repository, delivering @TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	SOURCE "DESC 7 amended in pull request #65 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B73, on"
		+ "the user's ruling at its refinement: every function, private ones included, proven by a"
		+ "guard"
		REF @TASK.B73

DECISION PluginsAreReachedByNameThroughOneResolverAndNeverImported
	TITLE "client, forge, scheduler, collector, check and output are plugin kinds resolved by name"
		+ "through one resolver; the core sees documents only and imports no plugin; Clean"
		+ "Architecture's layering is not adopted"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a built-in plugin is a module under its kind's package, an external one an executable"
		+ "brigade-<kind>-<name> on PATH for the client kind; the forge and the scheduler kinds"
		+ "resolve their built-in modules alone until @TASK.B76, post-MVP, delivers their"
		+ "executables; one resolver turns a name into one object answering the kind's operations,"
		+ "searched in the kind's declared order: project, machine, PATH, built-ins"
		REF @TASK.B76
	DESC "an operation takes a JSON-compatible dict and returns one, validated by the core on entry"
		+ "as @DECISION.DocumentsCarryAnIntegerSchemaVersionAndAreValidatedOnEntry sets; a module"
		+ "plugin and an executable plugin are indistinguishable to the core; no plugin Python type"
		+ "crosses"
		REF @DECISION.DocumentsCarryAnIntegerSchemaVersionAndAreValidatedOnEntry
	DESC "a client adapter translates: launch answers argv, environment and stdin, result parses"
		+ "the client's output into the normalised document; the core spawns and owns the process"
	DESC "no module outside a plugin package imports a plugin package statically; the resolver"
		+ "imports by name at run time; a plugin may import the core; the guard of tests/guards"
		+ "parses every module with ast and fails on a static import of brigade.adapters,"
		+ "brigade.collectors, brigade.checks or brigade.outputs from outside their own package,"
		+ "the guard @TASK.B42 asks for, widened"
		REF @TASK.B42
	DESC "cli.py builds the runtime, once per command and once per round of tick --loop through a"
		+ "factory it hands that command: paths, clock, process runner, spawner, resolver; the"
		+ "renderers of a command are declared by its module, as"
		+ "@DECISION.EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable sets; the"
		+ "commands resolve the plugins through the runtime's resolver, and a core function"
		+ "receives resolved plugin objects as arguments and resolves nothing itself, as @TASK.B73"
		+ "delivers"
		REF @DECISION.EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable
		REF @TASK.B73
	DESC "binds @TASK.B06, @TASK.B07, @TASK.B12, @TASK.B14, @TASK.B23, @TASK.B24, @TASK.B42,"
		+ "@TASK.B43, @TASK.B46, @TASK.B47 and @TASK.B48"
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B12
		REF @TASK.B14
		REF @TASK.B23
		REF @TASK.B24
		REF @TASK.B42
		REF @TASK.B43
		REF @TASK.B46
		REF @TASK.B47
		REF @TASK.B48
	REJECTED "a typing.Protocol shared by core and adapters in a common module: an adapter needs no"
		+ "brigade import to answer documents, and the graph stays one-directional"
	REJECTED "calling brigade adapter as a subprocess for a built-in adapter: a process per"
		+ "operation for a module already held; the executable path exists for external adapters"
	REJECTED "Clean Architecture's use case, presenter and ViewModel layering: one delivery"
		+ "mechanism, the command line of DESC 1 of the decision"
		+ "ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles, one persistence, neutral files,"
		+ "adapters already process-shaped, and a port at M3 that carries the contract, not the"
		+ "Python; the rules of the areas architecture and architecture_layers of the instructions"
		+ "corpus govern a core- package, which brigade is not"
	REJECTED "a core function handed a name and the runtime's resolver, the alternative F3 of the"
		+ "foundations review offers: the core would still resolve, and a resolved object passed as"
		+ "an argument is what a unit test replaces with a double"
	REJECTED "a renderer carried by the runtime: no core function renders, the renderers being"
		+ "declared by each command module in its record since pull request #56"
	RATIONALE "it refines DESC 5 and 6 of"
		+ "@DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles, DESC 3 of"
		+ "@DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters and plan section 17 to every plugin"
		+ "kind; a shared adapter is created by a factory, never at import, as the rule"
		+ "shared_adapter_created_explicitly of the instructions corpus says"
		REF @DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	RATIONALE "it departs from the architecture rules of the instructions corpus, the areas"
		+ "architecture and architecture_layers, stated here because this corpus declares no"
		+ "DEROGATES field: those rules govern a core- package, and brigade is a command-line tool"
		+ "with one delivery, one persistence and process-shaped adapters"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of @TASK.B73, amending DESC 5"
		REF @TASK.B73
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of @TASK.B76, amending DESC 1: an"
		+ "executable forge or scheduler is post-MVP comfort, F7 of the foundations review"
		REF @TASK.B76
	REJECTED "a unit test of run_segment patching spawn_process in its module: a global module"
		+ "mock, which the rule production_signature_not_deformed_for_test of the instructions"
		+ "corpus refuses; the runtime carries the spawner as it carries the process runner"
	SOURCE "the spawner added to DESC 5 in pull request #65 of the brigade repository, delivering"
		+ "@TASK.B73"
		REF @TASK.B73

DECISION TheTickIsAPurePlannerAndAnExecutorThatRecordsEveryAction
	TITLE "the tick builds one snapshot of the facts, plans its actions as a pure function of that"
		+ "snapshot, and applies them through an executor that records every outcome in the ledger"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a tick builds one snapshot of the facts, ledger-derived states, registry, git facts,"
		+ "forge facts, live processes and now, as frozen dataclasses; the snapshot serialises to"
		+ "one JSON document"
	DESC "plan(snapshot) -> actions is pure: no I/O, no clock, no randomness; an action is a frozen"
		+ "record, launch run, create worktree, merge pull request, pause wave, record event and"
		+ "the like"
	DESC "the executor applies the actions in order through the gateways and plugins handed to it,"
		+ "records each outcome in the ledger and stops at the first failure; the next tick"
		+ "recomputes from facts, so every action is idempotent or guarded by a fact"
	DESC "a tick runs plan and apply rounds until the plan is empty or a cap is reached, so a merge"
		+ "makes its dependents startable in the same tick, as @TASK.B17 asks"
		REF @TASK.B17
	DESC "brigade tick --dry-run prints the snapshot and the plan and applies nothing; a snapshot"
		+ "fixture file is the input of the planner's tests, table-driven on literal rows"
	DESC "due studies and due orders are the same shape: due is a pure function of schedule, last"
		+ "run and now"
	DESC "the tick keeps no truth of its own: the heartbeat of the last tick of @TASK.B28 is a"
		+ "state file written atomically, not a ledger line per empty tick"
		REF @TASK.B28
	DESC "binds @TASK.B07, @TASK.B12, @TASK.B14, @TASK.B17, @TASK.B18, @TASK.B19, @TASK.B48 and"
		+ "@TASK.B51"
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B12
		REF @TASK.B14
		REF @TASK.B17
		REF @TASK.B18
		REF @TASK.B19
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B51
	REJECTED "an imperative tick with injected gateways: every test needs a fake git, a fake forge"
		+ "and a fake ledger where the planner needs one JSON file"
	REJECTED "a tick state file as the truth: the facts are in the ledger, git, the forge and the"
		+ "corpora, as the decision ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent sets; a state"
		+ "file is derived"
	RATIONALE "every transition of @DECISION.ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent is a"
		+ "condition evaluated from facts, and @DECISION.CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge"
		+ "leaves no judgement to the tick; the rules test_static_data and test_quality of the"
		+ "instructions corpus want literal rows and time controlled, which a pure planner over a"
		+ "snapshot gives"
		REF @DECISION.ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent
		REF @DECISION.CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"

DECISION EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable
	TITLE "every command returns one document carrying schema_version, printed as JSON or rendered"
		+ "once as text, and exits by one table of codes mapped in cli.py from the exceptions run"
		+ "raises"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a command module exports one function named after the module, (request, runtime) ->"
		+ "document, a JSON-compatible dict carrying schema_version, or raises, an error or a"
		+ "stand-down, and returns none; --json prints it; the text is rendered from the document,"
		+ "so the text never shows a fact the document lacks"
	DESC "a document is bounded: a long result goes to a file under $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/ and"
		+ "the document carries its path and a summary; the journal of a run, brigade runs show"
		+ "<id> --log, is bounded record by record and its length is the run's, the reader taking"
		+ "its tail, as"
		+ "@DECISION.ARunKeepsAJournalOfOneShortTimestampedRecordPerActionThatTheReaderTails sets;"
		+ "brigade roles show <slot> returns the resolved role file whole, a text handed whole to a"
		+ "client, and --short bounds it to the front matter and the size of the body, from"
		+ "@TASK.B110"
		REF @DECISION.ARunKeepsAJournalOfOneShortTimestampedRecordPerActionThatTheReaderTails
		REF @TASK.B110
	DESC "stdout carries the document only; stderr carries diagnostics and errors; under --json an"
		+ "error still goes to stderr and stdout stays empty, awawa's convention"
	DESC "exit codes: 0 done, or stood down: another run holds the lock the command needs, one"
		+ "stderr line and stdout empty; 1 the command did not do what was asked, findings, a"
		+ "failed check, a missing prerequisite or a tool failure, with the document when there is"
		+ "one and a stderr line when there is not; 2 usage; 3 refused by policy; 4 paused on"
		+ "quota; 70 brigade's own defect, an unexpected exception with its traceback on stderr,"
		+ "sysexits EX_SOFTWARE"
	DESC "one exception family maps to the table, BrigadeError 1, UsageError 2, PolicyRefusal 3,"
		+ "QuotaPause 4, and StandingDown 0 outside that family, caught in cli.py alone; the"
		+ "message reads brigade <command>: <message>; findings are a document, not an exception"
	DESC "--json and the common options are declared once on a parent parser attached to every"
		+ "subcommand; brigade --version with or without --json stays as @TASK.B01 delivered it"
		REF @TASK.B01
	DESC "a long-lived command, tick --loop or serve, writes diagnostics to stderr and exits 0 on"
		+ "SIGTERM and SIGINT; brigade keeps no log file of its own besides runs/<id>/; the"
		+ "scheduler adapter decides where stderr goes, the journal or the file the cron line"
		+ "names; the cron line discards the stdout of each tick, its document, which the heartbeat"
		+ "tick.json already records"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B02 first, which introduces the renderer, the exit mapping, the parent parser"
		+ "and the runtime builder, then every command task"
		REF @TASK.B02
	DESC "brigade corpus given -- <awawa args> is the one command that passes another tool's"
		+ "stdout, stderr and exit code through unchanged: its reader is a person at a terminal,"
		+ "brigade's own readers call the gateway; without those args it returns its document, as"
		+ "@TASK.B08 sets"
		REF @TASK.B08
	REJECTED "three codes 0, 1 and 2: the plan's reference already documents 3 and 4 for the wave"
		+ "commands, and a crash exiting 1 passes for findings in a test and under systemd"
	REJECTED "an error document on stdout under --json: awawa, which the agents already read,"
		+ "prints errors on stderr; two conventions on one machine"
	REJECTED "a stand-down as a BrigadeError exiting 1: a timer firing while a long tick holds the"
		+ "lock is the normal case, and systemd and cron would record every such firing as a"
		+ "failure"
	REJECTED "the tick's stdout appended to tick.log with 2>&1 on the cron line: a text document"
		+ "every five minutes in the file meant for diagnostics, which the heartbeat already"
		+ "records; left to cron, stdout is mailed to the user at every firing"
	REJECTED "replacing argparse's usage exit: its exit 2 and usage message are the table's row,"
		+ "and the tests of B01 pin them"
	RATIONALE "the plan's exit-code line of the Blueprint, plan section 16, reads 0 done, 1"
		+ "findings, 2 usage, 3 refused by policy, 4 paused on quota; section 16 also bounds a"
		+ "document; the rules cli_exit_codes_and_streams, cli_parsing_handling_rendering_separated"
		+ "and cli_arguments_validated of the instructions corpus shape the rest"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "DESC 9 added on the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 in the refinement of B08"
	SOURCE "the stand-down of DESC 4 and 5 added in pull request #21 of the brigade repository,"
		+ "which delivers @TASK.B07; the stdout of the cron line in DESC 7 on the user's ruling of"
		+ "2026-10-06 in the review of that pull request"
		REF @TASK.B07
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 after wave M0: command modules follow"
		+ "one_exported_function_per_file, pull request #26"
	DESC "brigade tick --loop is the one catch outside cli.py: each tick runs through"
		+ "run_reporting_failure, a BrigadeError one stderr line, any other exception its"
		+ "traceback, and the loop ticks again; the table applies to the exit of the loop"
		REF @TASK.B56
	DESC "a command module declares, as a module-level constant of the frozen record type of"
		+ "brigade/command.py, the path, the help and the arguments of its one command line, its"
		+ "request reader, its text renderer, its exit decision and, where it has them, its"
		+ "Markdown renderer, its diagnostics, the renderer of the stderr a passthrough passes and"
		+ "the acceptance of extra arguments; the help of a group with no command of its own is"
		+ "declared by the records of its lines; cli.py renders and exits through the record alone,"
		+ "from @TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	SOURCE "the declared record of DESC 11 on the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 in the refinement of"
		+ "@TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	DESC "a group parser takes the common options as every command parser does: brigade project"
		+ "--json list runs, from @TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	DESC "brigade --help and the help of a group list their command lines in the order of their"
		+ "module names, from @TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	DESC "a group names its command lines action in its usage and its errors, from @TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	REJECTED "an order field in the record to keep the hand-written order of the help: a table of"
		+ "commands spread over the records, which discovery replaces"
	REJECTED "the common options on the adapter group alone, as the hand-written parsers of cli.py"
		+ "declared them: nothing kept them off the other groups, and DESC 6 attaches them to every"
		+ "subcommand"
	SOURCE "DESC 12 to 14 in pull request #56 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B82,"
		+ "validated by the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 in its review: \"Garder\" for the common"
		+ "options of a group, \"Valider\" for the order of the help and the name action"
		REF @TASK.B82
	DESC "the text of a list command is a table: a header row naming its columns, each column but"
		+ "the last padded to its widest cell, rendered by brigade/system/render_table.py; an empty"
		+ "list keeps its one-line message, from @TASK.B82"
		REF @TASK.B82
	SOURCE "DESC 15 on the user's words of 2026-10-07 in the review of pull request #56: \"il"
		+ "faudrait aussi que ça s'affiche dans un tableau à entête non?\""
		REF @TASK.B82
	SOURCE "DESC 2 amended for the journal of a run on the user's rulings of 2026-10-09 in the"
		+ "refinement of @TASK.B79"
		REF @TASK.B79
	SOURCE "DESC 2 amended for brigade roles show on the user's rulings of 2026-10-09 in the"
		+ "refinement of @TASK.B110"
		REF @TASK.B110

DECISION StateIsWrittenAtomicallyUnderLocksKeptInTheStateDirectory
	TITLE "shared state is written atomically under fcntl locks kept in the state directory, one"
		+ "lock file per shared resource: the tick, the ledger, each corpus repository and each"
		+ "project's worktrees"
	STATUS active
	DESC "locks are fcntl.flock on files under $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/locks/, one per shared"
		+ "resource: the tick, the ledger, each corpus repository brigade writes, keyed by path,"
		+ "and each project's worktrees; the PID is written for diagnosis, never used for exclusion"
	DESC "the tick takes its lock non-blocking; when another holds it, it exits 0 with one stderr"
		+ "line and records nothing"
	DESC "a ledger write is one line appended under the ledger lock, flushed before release; the"
		+ "file is never rewritten"
	DESC "a JSON state file is written to a temporary file in the same directory, fsynced and"
		+ "renamed over the old one; a reader meets a whole file or none"
	DESC "a corpus write, edit, fmt, lint and commit, runs under the repository's lock and is"
		+ "rolled back with git when lint fails, the one correction request of @TASK.B10"
		REF @TASK.B10
	DESC "the refs cache of brigade corpus has its lock,"
		+ "$XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/locks/refs-cache.lock: every placing, mark and removal of a"
		+ "cached tree runs under it"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B04, @TASK.B05, @TASK.B07, @TASK.B08, @TASK.B13 and @TASK.B22"
		REF @TASK.B04
		REF @TASK.B05
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B08
		REF @TASK.B13
		REF @TASK.B22
	REJECTED "locks under $XDG_CACHE_HOME, the Blueprint plan's place: a cache may be deleted at"
		+ "any time, and a deleted lock file breaks the exclusion"
	REJECTED "PID-liveness or mkdir locks: the kernel releases flock when the process dies; no"
		+ "stale-lock code to write or test"
	REJECTED "relying on O_APPEND atomicity: true on Linux for one write call, unspecified"
		+ "elsewhere; the lock costs microseconds"
	RATIONALE "DESC 4 of @DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites names only the"
		+ "refs and the collector caches for $XDG_CACHE_HOME and puts state under $XDG_STATE_HOME,"
		+ "so locks in the state directory contradict no decision; @TASK.B13 promotes the ledger"
		+ "from parallel runs"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites
		REF @TASK.B13
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 during wave M0, pull request #23 of the brigade"
		+ "repository"

DECISION ShippedFilesLiveInsideThePackageAndAreReadAsResources
	TITLE "every file brigade ships lives in a data/ folder of the component that reads it, under"
		+ "brigade/, and is read with importlib.resources, so the clone and the zipapp read the"
		+ "same files"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every file brigade ships, the operational schema template, the built-in roles,"
		+ "procedures, recipes and templates, the dashboard page and the scheduler unit templates,"
