DECISION OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa
	TITLE "every subprocess goes through one runner of brigade/system, git and awawa through"
		+ "gateway modules built on it, and gh through the GitHub forge adapter alone"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every subprocess goes through one function of brigade/system: an argv list, never a shell"
		+ "string, an explicit cwd, an environment built from a whitelist, PATH, HOME, LANG, LC_*,"
		+ "XDG_*, the BRIGADE_* variables of collectors, COVERAGE_PROCESS_CONFIG when brigade's own"
		+ "environment carries it, and what the adapter adds, a timeout on every call, UTF-8 text"
		+ "with replacement; it returns a record, argv, cwd, exit code, stdout, stderr and"
		+ "duration, and raises ToolFailure on an exit code the caller did not declare acceptable,"
		+ "awawa lint 1 or gh pr view 1 on not found"
	DESC "the runner builds that environment through brigade/system/build_process_environment, its"
		+ "environment module, exported alone: run_process and build_process_environment are, with"
		+ "paths, the modules the environment-read guard of"
		+ "@DECISION.PathsAndConfigurationAreResolvedInOnePlaceFromXdgVariables allows"
		REF @DECISION.PathsAndConfigurationAreResolvedInOnePlaceFromXdgVariables
	DESC "git and awawa have gateway modules, brigade/git/ and brigade/corpus/, exposing named"
		+ "operations built on the runner; nothing else calls git or awawa; gh is called only by"
		+ "the GitHub forge adapter"
	DESC "a detached run is spawned by one function: new session, stdout and stderr to files under"
		+ "runs/<id>/, pid file; liveness is read from the pid and the result file"
	DESC "--verbose prints every subprocess argv, exit code and duration on stderr"
	DESC "a gateway is tested in tests/integration against a real git repository or awawa corpus in"
		+ "a temporary directory; a fake executable on PATH doubles a tool only when its failure is"
		+ "the behaviour under test, the PATH of fixture executables of @TASK.B02"
		REF @TASK.B02
	DESC "binds @TASK.B02, @TASK.B04, @TASK.B06, @TASK.B08, @TASK.B13 and @TASK.B47"
		REF @TASK.B02
		REF @TASK.B04
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B08
		REF @TASK.B13
		REF @TASK.B47
	REJECTED "subprocess calls scattered where needed: no timeout policy, no environment policy,"
		+ "and a port must find them all"
	REJECTED "shell=True anywhere: quoting defects and a dependency on the user's shell"
	REJECTED "a COVERAGE_ prefix in the whitelist: patch = subprocess of coverage.py needs"
		+ "COVERAGE_PROCESS_CONFIG alone, and a prefix would pass the coverage settings of the"
		+ "user's shell to every tool"
	RATIONALE "the rule test_doubles of the instructions corpus prefers a real implementation when"
		+ "fast, deterministic and isolated, and repository_facts_proven_by_command wants the"
		+ "command that proves a fact: one runner records every call, and real git and awawa in a"
		+ "temporary directory answer the gateway tests"
	RATIONALE "COVERAGE_PROCESS_CONFIG is how coverage.py, under patch = subprocess, reaches a"
		+ "child; without it a detached run or an external adapter launched by brigade under the"
		+ "coverage job of @TASK.B66 is never measured, and outside that job the variable is unset,"
		+ "so the whitelist passes nothing more"
		REF @TASK.B66
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 on pull request #24 of the brigade repository: one"
		+ "export per module, the environment of the runner in a module of its own"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 on pull request #44 of the brigade repository, \"je"
		+ "veux que ça soit fait dans la même pr\": COVERAGE_PROCESS_CONFIG passed to the children"
		+ "when brigade's own environment carries it"

DECISION TheClockIsReadOnceAndCarriedAsAFact
	TITLE "now is read once per command, or per tick of a loop, in UTC, and carried as a fact in"
		+ "the request or the snapshot; no core function reads the clock, and one tick has one"
		+ "instant"
	STATUS active
	DESC "now is read once per command, or per tick of a loop, in the runtime, in UTC, and carried"
		+ "in the request or the snapshot; no core function reads the clock; one tick has one"
		+ "instant"
	DESC "a CLI test that needs the past writes facts in the past, a ledger line whose resume_at"
		+ "precedes now; the planner's tests pass now as a literal"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B05, @TASK.B07, @TASK.B19 and @TASK.B48"
		REF @TASK.B05
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B19
		REF @TASK.B48
	REJECTED "a BRIGADE_NOW override: an environment branch in production code, which the rule"
		+ "environment_difference_in_configuration of the instructions corpus refuses, for what a"
		+ "fixture can state"
	REJECTED "datetime.now() in core modules: two instants in one tick; the rule test_quality of"
		+ "the instructions corpus wants time controlled"
	RATIONALE "a time read once is a fact like any other of the snapshot: the planner stays pure"
		+ "and a test states the time it needs instead of controlling a clock"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"

DECISION PathsAndConfigurationAreResolvedInOnePlaceFromXdgVariables
	TITLE "the roots are built once from the XDG variables in brigade/system/paths, config.toml is"
		+ "read once into a frozen record, and every function takes the paths it needs as arguments"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade/system/paths builds the roots once from XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME and"
		+ "XDG_CACHE_HOME with their defaults; no module other than paths and the process runner of"
		+ "brigade/system, run_process and build_process_environment, its environment module, reads"
		+ "os.environ, os.getenv, Path.home or expanduser, a guard of tests/guards checks it; every"
		+ "function takes the paths it needs as arguments"
	DESC "tests redirect brigade with the XDG variables alone; no brigade-specific override"
		+ "variable"
	DESC "config.toml is read with tomllib into one frozen record with defaults; an unknown key or"
		+ "a wrong type is an error naming the key and the file; brigade writes it once at init"
		+ "from the shipped template and never rewrites it; doctor reports it"
	DESC "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/ is the operational corpus repository; config.toml is in its"
		+ ".gitignore, a machine binding not being a ratified fact, as"
		+ "@DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites rules; roles/, collectors/,"
		+ "checks/ and recipes/ are versioned with it"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites
	DESC "binds @TASK.B02, @TASK.B03, @TASK.B04, @TASK.B06, @TASK.B42 and @TASK.B43"
		REF @TASK.B02
		REF @TASK.B03
		REF @TASK.B04
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B42
		REF @TASK.B43
	DESC "brigade init creates the operational corpus repository and config.toml only; every writer"
		+ "creates its directory under $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/ or $XDG_CACHE_HOME/brigade/ when it"
		+ "writes"
	DESC "Paths exposes the paths shared by several components, configuration_file, lock_directory,"
		+ "heartbeat_file and schema_file, built from its roots; a file or directory name used by"
		+ "one component alone is declared in that component's module or its *_locations module"
		REF @TASK.B77
	DESC "only the command modules read config.toml, once per command, and pass the record down; a"
		+ "guard of tests/guards checks the calls of its readers; the purge of the trails is the"
		+ "one exception, as @DECISION.ATrailIsWrittenOnlyForWorkDoneAndThePurgeReadsTrailDaysAlone"
		+ "rules"
		REF @DECISION.ATrailIsWrittenOnlyForWorkDoneAndThePurgeReadsTrailDaysAlone
		REF @TASK.B77
	REJECTED "a BRIGADE_HOME variable: a second way to say what XDG already says"
	REJECTED "init creating the state and cache directories, the Blueprint plan's step: a writer"
		+ "relying on it breaks once the directory is deleted"
	REJECTED "the shared names as constants of a module of their own, joined by every caller to a"
		+ "root: each caller would still build the path, the join being what the decision places in"
		+ "one place"
	REJECTED "every file and directory name of brigade in one module: the names a single component"
		+ "uses are its own and stay beside it"
	REJECTED "a config set command rewriting the file: tomllib reads only; a writer without"
		+ "round-trip loses the user's comments"
	RATIONALE "DESC 3 and 4 of @DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites already"
		+ "place the machine bindings and the custom roles, collectors, checks and recipes under"
		+ "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/; one module turning the variables into paths is what keeps"
		+ "every other function free of the environment"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05 in the refinement of B03"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 on pull request #24 of the brigade repository: one"
		+ "export per module, the environment of the runner in a module of its own"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-09 at the refinement of B77: the shared names as derived"
		+ "paths of Paths; config.toml read in the command modules alone, under a guard"
		REF @TASK.B77

DECISION DocumentsCarryAnIntegerSchemaVersionAndAreValidatedOnEntry
	TITLE "every document brigade writes or reads carries an integer schema_version per kind, an"
		+ "inbound document is validated against its declared shape before the core reads it, and a"
		+ "reader upgrades every version ever written"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every document brigade writes or reads, command output, ledger line, result, collector"
		+ "document, recipe, config and answer file, carries schema_version, an integer per"
		+ "document kind starting at 1, the name @TASK.B01 and @TASK.B02 fix; @TASK.B47 and"
		+ "@TASK.B50 say schema and are aligned at their refinement"
		REF @TASK.B01
		REF @TASK.B02
		REF @TASK.B47
		REF @TASK.B50
	DESC "one validator module checks an inbound document, an adapter answer, a collector output, a"
		+ "plan JSON or a study answer, against a shape declared next to its kind, required keys,"
		+ "types and enumerations, before the core reads it; an unknown schema_version is refused"
		+ "by name"
	DESC "a reader keeps an upgrade function per kind from every version ever written to the"
		+ "current one; a ledger line is upgraded on read and never rewritten; a state file is"
		+ "upgraded on read and written back current"
	DESC "inside the core a document becomes a frozen dataclass; the module of its kind declares"
		+ "from_document when brigade reads the kind and to_document when brigade writes it, no"
		+ "function for a direction no code crosses; dicts stay at the edges"
	DESC "timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC with Z; durations are integer milliseconds in *_ms fields;"
		+ "run ids are time-sortable, <UTC compact>-<6 hex>, from one function"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B02, @TASK.B05, @TASK.B06, @TASK.B42, @TASK.B47, @TASK.B48 and @TASK.B50"
		REF @TASK.B02
		REF @TASK.B05
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B42
		REF @TASK.B47
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B50
	REJECTED "a schema string naming kind and version: the kind is already the event name, the"
		+ "collector name, the command or the file name, and two ratified tasks name schema_version"
	REJECTED "JSON Schema validated by a library: a third-party dependency for keys, types and"
		+ "enumerations"
	REJECTED "both functions for every kind: the snapshot of the tick is never read, and its"
		+ "from_document would be called by its test alone"
	RATIONALE "DESC 3 of @DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles gives every"
		+ "result, event, collector, recipe and config document a schema version and DESC 2 refuses"
		+ "pickle; SPEC 1 of @TASK.B01 and SPEC 3 of @TASK.B02 already name schema_version"
		REF @DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles
		REF @TASK.B01
		REF @TASK.B02
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of @TASK.B74: a kind carries only the"
		+ "directions it crosses, DESC 4 amended"
		REF @TASK.B74

DECISION TaskPullRequestCarriesTheGitHubMilestoneNamedByItsMilestoneTitle
	TITLE "the pull request of a task carries the GitHub milestone named after the TITLE of the"
		+ "task's MILESTONE"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the pull request delivering a task is assigned the GitHub milestone whose name is the"
		+ "TITLE of the task's MILESTONE: @TASK.B03 belongs to @MILESTONE.M0, TITLE Foundations, so"
		+ "its pull request carries the GitHub milestone Foundations"
		REF @TASK.B03
		REF @MILESTONE.M0
	REJECTED "the id of the corpus milestone, M0, as the name of the GitHub milestone: the user"
		+ "named Foundations, the TITLE"
	REJECTED "a rule of the instructions corpus binding every project: asked whether the ruling was"
		+ "general or brigade's, the user placed it in brigade"
	RATIONALE "the milestone view of GitHub groups the pull requests of a milestone; a pull request"
		+ "carrying none is easily left out of it"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 during the launch of wave M0"

DECISION ClientAdaptersAnswerEveryOperationThroughOneFunction
	TITLE "a client adapter answers every operation through one function, answer(operation,"
		+ "request), or as brigade-client-<name> <operation> with the request on stdin; the core"
		+ "completes each request and runs what the adapter only names"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a built-in client adapter is a module of brigade/adapters/clients, or of"
		+ "brigade/adapters/test_clients for an adapter of the test suite, exposing"
		+ "answer(operation, request); an external one is an executable run as"
		+ "brigade-client-<name> <operation>, the request as JSON on stdin and the answer as JSON"
		+ "on stdout; the operation names are those of brigade adapter: probe, launch-argv,"
		+ "parse-result, resume-argv, transcripts and actions"
	DESC "actions turns the new output of a segment, its complete lines since the last read, into"
		+ "the actions it holds, each a kind, tool, text or result, and a summary the core cuts to"
		+ "200 characters; the claude-code adapter launches its client with --output-format"
		+ "stream-json and --verbose, and reads parse-result from the last result event of the"
		+ "stream"
	DESC "the core completes every request with the reasoning table config.toml sets, the settings"
		+ "of the table [clients.<name>] of config.toml and the home directory brigade/system/paths"
		+ "builds; an adapter reads neither the environment nor config.toml"
	DESC "the probe names the command that prints the client's version, version_argv, null for an"
		+ "adapter with no client executable; brigade doctor runs it through the process runner"
	DESC "the fake adapter reads the directory of its recordings from the setting recordings of"
		+ "[clients.fake] and replays the recording named after the role, <recordings>/<role>.json"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B42 and every task that launches, resumes or reads a client: @TASK.B06,"
		+ "@TASK.B19, @TASK.B35 and @TASK.B45"
		REF @TASK.B42
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B19
		REF @TASK.B35
		REF @TASK.B45
	REJECTED "five exported functions per adapter module: the one-exported-function rule of the"
		+ "instructions corpus, and a module answering as the executable does keeps the two forms"
		+ "indistinguishable"
	REJECTED "an adapter spawning its client's version check in probe: the core spawns and owns"
		+ "every process, an adapter only translates"
	REJECTED "a top-level config.toml key for the fake's recordings: the core would name one"
		+ "adapter's setting; per-client tables carry any adapter's settings"
	RATIONALE "it applies @DECISION.PluginsAreReachedByNameThroughOneResolverAndNeverImported and"
		+ "@DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters to the client kind"
		REF @DECISION.PluginsAreReachedByNameThroughOneResolverAndNeverImported
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	RATIONALE "no rate-limit result was recorded on the reference machine on 2026-10-06; the reset"
		+ "hour is read from the forms resets 3pm, resets 10:30am (UTC) and resets at 14:00, and a"
		+ "message naming none leaves reset null, the fallback of"
		+ "@DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	SOURCE "pull request #16 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B42"
		REF @TASK.B42

DECISION ACorpusWriteFormatsAndRestoresOnlyTheFileBrigadeWrote
	TITLE "a corpus write formats, and on a failing lint restores, only the file brigade wrote; the"
		+ "lint runs on the whole corpus"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade runs awawa fmt on the file it wrote, never on the corpus root; awawa lint"
		+ "--strict runs on the corpus root"
	DESC "a failing lint restores that file from HEAD, or removes it when HEAD does not hold it,"
		+ "and nothing else"
	DESC "the transaction is brigade/corpus/change_corpus_file, under the lock of the corpus"
		+ "repository; binds @TASK.B04 and @TASK.B43"
		REF @TASK.B04
		REF @TASK.B43
	REJECTED "awawa fmt over the corpus root: it rewrites the files the user edited by hand, which"
		+ "the restore of one file then leaves rewritten and uncommitted"
	REJECTED "a checkout of the whole corpus on a failing lint: it discards the user's uncommitted"
		+ "edits"
	SOURCE "pull request #17 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B04"
		REF @TASK.B04

DECISION EveryRunIsHeldOnTheClockAtThirtySecondsPerStepOfItsCap
	TITLE "every run is cut on the clock of the machine at its step cap times seconds_per_step, 30"
		+ "by default, and a client that counts no steps is reported as held on the clock alone"
	STATUS active
	CLOSES @OPEN_QUESTION.WallTimeBudgetOfAClientThatCountsNoSteps
	DESC "the wall-time limit of a run is ceil(budget × 1.25) × seconds_per_step, the step cap of"
		+ "the Claude Code adapter times a config.toml key defaulting to 30 s; brigade measures it"
		+ "on the machine's clock, whatever the client"
	DESC "the limit holds every client, those that count their steps included, as a bound against a"
		+ "client stuck on a command"
	DESC "at the limit brigade sends SIGTERM to the client's process group and SIGKILL 30 s later;"
		+ "the segment ends with outcome wall_limit, distinct from the step cap"
	DESC "a client whose probe declares no step count is held by the clock alone: brigade doctor"
		+ "and brigade run warn so, and the supported-clients table shows the fallback"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B06 and @TASK.B49"
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B49
	REJECTED "20 s per step, the measured p90 rounded: a run of 77 steps would be cut at 1920 s,"
		+ "under the 2762 s of active time measured at most"
	REJECTED "a p90 of seconds per step read from the ledger per procedure: a client that counts no"
		+ "steps gives no denominator"
	REJECTED "a max_wall key in every procedure: a third required key repeating the budget;"
		+ "max_wall stays the recipes' own"
	REJECTED "a warning without a limit: a stuck client keeps its slot, and a run of 9 h was"
		+ "measured, mostly waiting"
	RATIONALE "686 unattended Claude Code subagent runs of this machine took 10.1 s per active step"
		+ "at the median and 18.1 s at p90, 2762 s of active time at most; 30 s per step covers"
		+ "that maximum for a run of p90 length; Codex exec, Gemini CLI and OpenCode document no"
		+ "run timeout, and agent harnesses set a wall limit per run as a backstop"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-06 in the refinement of B06, on the measurements of"
		+ "transcripts and the client documentation read that day"

DECISION ASlotIsBoundByTheSlotsTableOrByTheSlotItsRoleFileDeclares
	TITLE "the table [slots] of config.toml binds a slot to an AGENT entity; a machine role file"
		+ "takes the slot its front matter declares; a role file declares work beside the six keys"
		+ "of its first form"
	STATUS active
	DESC "[slots] maps a slot among the nine to the name of an AGENT entity of the instructions"
		+ "corpus; an unknown slot or a value that is no string is an error naming the key and the"
		+ "file; a row with no instructions key set is an error naming the row and the file"
	DESC "a file of the machine's roles directory, any name ending in .md, takes the slot its front"
		+ "matter declares; two files declaring one slot are an error naming both, and a finding of"
		+ "brigade roles lint on the later one"
	DESC "a role file declares name, slot, work, reasoning, capabilities, budget and returns; an"
		+ "AGENT entity fills work with its WORK lines and returns with its RETURNS lines joined by"
		+ "a semicolon, capabilities with its CAPABILITY lines joined by a comma"
	DESC "the body of an AGENT entity's role is awawa context @AGENT.<name> --depth 2 --skip"
		+ "reasoning on the instructions corpus, read at each resolution"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B43 and @TASK.B06, which applies PROJECT.ROLE ahead of these sources"
		REF @TASK.B43
		REF @TASK.B06
	REJECTED "a machine role file named after its slot, plan.md: the front matter already declares"
		+ "the slot, and two spellings of it could disagree"
	REJECTED "WORK left out of the front matter: the task's fourth SPEC names it among the fields"
		+ "that fill it, and no other key holds the work of a role"
	REJECTED "a key repeated once per value: a role file holds one key: value per line"
	SOURCE "pull request #20 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B43"
		REF @TASK.B43

