DECISION ARunKeepsOneDirectoryWithAFolderPerSegmentAndItsResultWrittenLast
	TITLE "a run keeps one directory under runs/<id>/ for all its segments, one folder"
		+ "segments/<n>/ per segment, and result.json written last marks it finished"
	STATUS active
	DESC "runs/<id>/ holds run.json, the record of the run as planned, pid, role.md, progress.md,"
		+ "journal.jsonl, the journal of the actions of every segment, segments/<n>/ with brief.md,"
		+ "stdout.log, stderr.log and result.json, the normalised result of that segment, and"
		+ "result.json, the normalised result of the last segment"
	DESC "result.json is written atomically after the ledger events of the run: a run with a result"
		+ "is finished, one whose pid lives without it is running, any other is dead"
	DESC "a hand-over keeps the run id and numbers the segment; the brief of segment n opens on the"
		+ "progress file"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B06, and every task that reads a run, @TASK.B07 and @TASK.B19"
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B19
	REJECTED "a new run id per segment: the ledger's segment field and runs list would split one"
		+ "run into several, and the progress file would move at each hand-over"
	REJECTED "one stdout.log and stderr.log appended across segments: runs logs could no longer"
		+ "tell which segment printed a line, and the brief each segment received would be lost"
	REJECTED "a state file rewritten as the run advances: the pid and the result already answer"
		+ "running, finished and dead, without a write a crash could leave half done"
	SOURCE "pull request #24 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B06"
		REF @TASK.B06

