DECISION APullRequestTouchingOnlyTheCorpusOrDocumentationRunsNoCodeJob
	TITLE "a pull request touching only corpus/, docs/, artifact/ or Markdown at the root starts no"
		+ "job of ci.yml; a push to main runs them all"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the pull_request trigger of .github/workflows/ci.yml carries paths-ignore corpus/**,"
		+ "docs/**, artifact/** and *.md, the Markdown at the root alone: a pull request changing"
		+ "only those files starts none of its jobs, a pull request changing one other file starts"
		+ "them all"
	DESC "the push trigger on main carries no filter: every merge runs the whole suite"
	DESC "no job of ci.yml reads those paths: the tests write their own corpora in temporary"
		+ "directories, and no .awawa file lies outside corpus/"
	DESC "the corpus job of @TASK.B95 lives in a workflow of its own, which runs on every pull"
		+ "request as DESC 3 of @DECISION.TheCiInstallsAwawaFromAPrivateReleaseAndNoTestSkipsThere"
		+ "sets, so that a pull request touching only corpus/ is still checked"
		REF @TASK.B95
		REF @DECISION.TheCiInstallsAwawaFromAPrivateReleaseAndNoTestSkipsThere
	REJECTED "a first job detecting the changed paths and an if: on every job: about fifteen lines"
		+ "of YAML for checks reported skipped, which matter only under required status checks, and"
		+ "main has no branch protection"
	REJECTED "a paths list of the files that start the CI: a file forgotten in the list skips the"
		+ "CI without a warning, where a paths-ignore list starts it for every new kind of file"
	RATIONALE "a pull request of refinement, such as pull request #58 changing corpus/ alone, ran"
		+ "the eight jobs of ci.yml, tests on two Pythons, the floor, zizmor, ruff, semgrep,"
		+ "vulture and coverage, none of which reads a file it changed"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07: paths-ignore of the workflow rather than a detecting"
		+ "job or a paths list, delivered by a pull request of its own without a task"

DECISION ATrailIsWrittenOnlyForWorkDoneAndThePurgeReadsTrailDaysAlone
	TITLE "the trail of a command is written at its end when it ran a subprocess, the trail of a"
		+ "tick once it holds the lock, and the purge of the trails reads trail_days alone"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the records of a command other than run and tick are held until its end, its error path"
		+ "included, and written to commands/<instant>-<command>.jsonl only when it ran a"
		+ "subprocess"
	DESC "the trail of a tick is created once the tick holds the lock, so a tick that stands down"
		+ "writes nothing; tick --dry-run is no tick, and its records go to the trail of its"
		+ "command"
	DESC "the purge parses config.toml itself and reads trail_days alone through read_trail_days:"
		+ "no file means 7 days, a file that is not TOML or a trail_days that is no integer of 1 or"
		+ "more keeps every trail, the other keys are not read"
	DESC "a trail_days that is no integer of 1 or more is an error of read_configuration alone,"
		+ "which brigade doctor reports as a finding naming the key and the file"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B72"
		REF @TASK.B72
	REJECTED "the purge through read_configuration: a config.toml off its shape, client = 1, then"
		+ "fails every command before it runs, brigade doctor included, whose work is to name that"
		+ "defect"
	REJECTED "trail_days the only key allowed to stop every command: a trail_days off its shape"
		+ "then fails every command before it runs, brigade doctor and brigade init included, whose"
		+ "work is to name and repair that defect"
	REJECTED "the trail of a tick located before the lock: a tick that stands down would leave an"
		+ "empty trail where tick --once writes nothing"
	REJECTED "an empty trail for a command that started no subprocess: a file holding no record,"
		+ "nothing for the reader of the trails to read"
	RATIONALE "brigade doctor names a configuration off its shape, so no command may fail on it"
		+ "before doctor runs"
	SOURCE "pull request #60 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-07 on the review of pull request #60, \"option A\": the"
		+ "purge keeps every trail on a trail_days it cannot read, read_configuration keeps"
		+ "reporting the error and doctor names it"

DECISION ForgeAccountsAreBoundPerSlotAndThePolicyChoosesTheReviewMode
	TITLE "config.toml binds a forge login per slot and one for brigade's own gh calls;"
		+ "POLICY.REVIEW chooses approval, verdict or local delivery"
	STATUS active
	DESC "[forge_accounts] of config.toml maps a slot, or the key cli for the gh subprocesses"
		+ "brigade starts itself, to a gh login; a process acting for a bound key carries GH_TOKEN,"
		+ "the token gh auth token --user <login> prints, and an unbound one acts as gh's active"
		+ "account"
	DESC "a bound login whose token gh does not print after forge_attempts attempts stops the"
		+ "command on an error, records the ledger event forge_account_unavailable and pauses the"
		+ "wave; no other account is used in its place; once the preflight exists it checks the"
		+ "logins before a wave"
	DESC "every write to the forge records in its ledger event the login it ran as"
	DESC "POLICY.REVIEW sets the review mode of a project: verdict, the default, the verdict of the"
		+ "verify slot recorded in the ledger and the merge into integration needing no GitHub"
		+ "approval; approval, the verify slot posting a review that approves or requests changes"
		+ "under its login, distinct from the login of the build slot, and the merge waiting for"
		+ "the approval; local, the tasks merged into integration on the machine and one pull"
		+ "request from integration to main opened once the wave is delivered"
	DESC "a prudence run verifies every task in each mode, as"
		+ "@DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate sets; under local it verifies"
		+ "the task branch before its merge on the machine"
		REF @DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
	REJECTED "one forge account for every write, the key forge_account config.toml accepted until"
		+ "now: GitHub refuses an approval by the author of a pull request, so a verify slot cannot"
		+ "approve the pull request its build slot opened under the same account"
	REJECTED "forge_account as the default login and [forge_accounts] overriding a slot: the user"
		+ "ruled the table alone, one place naming every login"
	REJECTED "the runs of the client without a token, the pull request opened under the user's"
		+ "active account: the user ruled that the login of the build slot opens it"
	REJECTED "a fallback to gh's active account when a bound login has no token: reviews and merges"
		+ "would run as the user's account, which the branch protection of plan section 18 cannot"
		+ "tell from the bot"
	REJECTED "approval as the default mode: it needs two bot accounts, where verdict runs with one"
	REJECTED "the review mode as a field of PROJECT: how far a project's waves run on their own"
		+ "belongs with AUTO_MERGE in POLICY"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled that brigade adapts to at least three workflows: prudence approving"
		+ "under a bot account distinct from the build account, pull requests merged without"
		+ "approval, and every task delivered on the machine with one pull request once the tasks"
		+ "are delivered; delivered by @TASK.B75, @TASK.B99 and @TASK.B100"
		REF @TASK.B75
		REF @TASK.B99
		REF @TASK.B100
	SOURCE "the user's words of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of B75, \"il faut permettre 2"
		+ "workflow: soit on décide que prudence doit approuver, et dans ce cas on doit lui"
		+ "attacher un compte bot différent du compte de build, soit on décide que les PR seront"
		+ "mergées sans passer par des approvals\"; \"Refuser oui. La vérification de la"
		+ "disponibilité du compte devra se faire en amont (en preflight quand on l'aura"
		+ "implémenté). Si un incident arrive en cours de route, on devra prévoir des attemps pour"
		+ "retry. Et si tout échoue, la run s'arrête avec une erreur critique.\""

DECISION EveryEndOfARunHasItsOwnExitCodeRangedBySeverity
	TITLE "every end of a run has an outcome and an exit code of its own: 0 delivered, 1 to 9"
		+ "errors, 10 to 19 warnings, 20 to 29 normal operation without delivery"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade never infers done: a segment is done only when the run declares it, and every"
		+ "other end, an end the run did not declare included, has its outcome and its code"
	DESC "0 done; 1 failed, an error of the client; 2 a usage error; 3 undeclared, a segment ended"
		+ "without the run's declaration of its end"
	DESC "10 blocked, the run waits for a ruling; 11 wall_limit; 12 turn_limit"
	DESC "20 handed_over, the run handed over and no hand-over is left"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B102"
		REF @TASK.B102
	REJECTED "a code written only for done, its absence meaning a run still in progress: a run"
		+ "ending on an unknown cause would leave its caller waiting for a done that never comes"
	REJECTED "done at 20 with the other normal codes: the shell, systemd and cron read every code"
		+ "but 0 as a failure"
	REJECTED "one code shared by every end that is not done, or 1 for all of them as B06 does after"
		+ "the last hand-over: a caller such as the tick could not tell a client error from a"
		+ "budget too tight without reading the result"
	RATIONALE "the ranges follow the user's comparison with HTTP status codes, ordered from the"
		+ "most to the least severe; 70, the last resort of brigade/cli.py for an unexpected"
		+ "exception, is left outside them"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 at the drafting of B102, \"toute sortie doit donner"
		+ "lieu à un code\" and \"de 1 à 9 les erreurs, à partir de 10 les warnings et à partir de"
		+ "20 les codes de fonctionnement normal\""

DECISION ARunDeclaresTheEndOfEachSegmentOnTheLastLineOfItsFinalMessage
	TITLE "a run declares how each segment ends on the last line of its final message, and brigade"
		+ "reads that declaration instead of detecting a run still in progress"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the brief announces the line brigade-end: <done|handed_over|blocked>; the adapter reads"
		+ "the last line of the final message the segment's log holds; any other last line is"
		+ "undeclared"
	DESC "a segment ending on undeclared is relaunched on the same count of POLICY.HANDOVERS as a"
		+ "hand-over"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B102"
		REF @TASK.B102
	REJECTED "detecting a hand-over from the progress file, a HANDOVER section or a non-empty file:"
		+ "the file is written after each step and kept at completion, and the section is a"
		+ "convention of the author's instructions, not of brigade"
	REJECTED "a marker line in the progress file: it outlives the segment that wrote it, and"
		+ "brigade would have to strip it before each relaunch"
	REJECTED "a file of its own for the declaration: the adapter would grant a second write beyond"
		+ "the role's capabilities"
	REJECTED "the last brigade-end: line anywhere in the log: a tool output quoting the line would"
		+ "be read as the declaration"
	REJECTED "a count of its own in POLICY for undeclared segments: two bounds on the segments of"
		+ "one run"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 at the drafting of B102, \"il faut qu'on trouve plutôt"
		+ "un moyen d'enregistrer un marqueur de finition plutôt que d'essayer de détecter si on"
		+ "est toujours en progression\""

DECISION EveryDocumentBrigadeReadsBackAcceptsAnAwawaFormAndTextIsARenderingHandedWhole
	TITLE "every document brigade reads back or parses accepts an awawa form through the plugin"
		+ "kind document; text stays the form of a rendering handed whole to a client, to GitHub or"
		+ "to a person, produced from the entities"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every document brigade reads back or parses, the progress of a run, a role file, a"
		+ "procedure file, a wave report, a study answer and an order output, accepts an awawa form"
		+ "beside its Markdown form, served by the plugin kind document that @TASK.B106 introduces:"
		+ "every operation of the kind takes the document it serves, its path, its schema resource"
		+ "and its frame; a document brigade reads later names its two forms, its schema and its"
		+ "frame when it is specified"
		REF @TASK.B106
	DESC "the awawa form is read entity by entity, status, show and context on the file, never the"
		+ "file whole; the sections a command fills are fields, the narrative a prose field; the"
		+ "schema is shipped by brigade as a resource of its package under a name not ending in"
		+ ".awawa, as @DECISION.ShippedFilesLiveInsideThePackageAndAreReadAsResources sets, and"
		+ "read from no instructions corpus"
		REF @DECISION.ShippedFilesLiveInsideThePackageAndAreReadAsResources
	DESC "a document in its awawa form is validated by awawa lint against that schema, never by a"
		+ "comparison of its headings; a field a command filled is one the answer may not change"
	DESC "a document whose code does not exist yet is designed as entities from the start, its"
		+ "Markdown a rendering for the person and for the dashboard: @TASK.B20, @TASK.B31,"
		+ "@TASK.B48, @TASK.B50 and @TASK.B51 are amended so; the role and the procedure files,"
		+ "whose Markdown form works, gain the awawa form by @TASK.B107"
		REF @TASK.B20
		REF @TASK.B31
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B50
		REF @TASK.B51
		REF @TASK.B107
	DESC "text stays the form of the brief of a segment, segments/<n>/brief.md, of the role file"
		+ "passed to the client, runs/<id>/role.md, and of the file of --brief: a client takes only"
		+ "text, and brigade reads none of the three back"
	DESC "text stays the form of the body of a pull request, of a review reply and of the adapter"
		+ "matrix of the README: GitHub and a person read them, brigade parses none"
	DESC "text stays the form of the dated documents of docs/: a dated document is never rewritten,"
		+ "as the rule dated_document_never_rewritten of the instructions corpus sets, and brigade"
		+ "reads none"
	DESC "a text rendering is produced from the entities, as awawa context renders an AGENT entity"
		+ "into the body of a role, and shows no fact its entities lack"
	REJECTED "Markdown kept as the one form of every document, its sections found by headings: a"
		+ "file read whole costs its length at every read, and a comparison of headings validates"
		+ "nothing of the content"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-07 that everything that is a .md must be manageable"
		+ "through awawa instead, and approved the plan of this decision, of @TASK.B107 and of the"
		+ "amendments; the inventory of that day found the brief of a segment, the role file and"
		+ "the file of --brief never read back, brigade/runs/run_segment.py:65-66,"
		+ "brigade/adapters/clients/claude_code.py:65-73 and brigade/runs/plan_run.py:117-123, the"
		+ "progress of a run already served by @TASK.B106, no code of the reports yet, and the"
		+ "triage, the intake and the wave plans already JSONL or entities"
		REF @TASK.B106
		REF @TASK.B107
	RATIONALE "the user wants brigade operational quickly: a form that already works is not"
		+ "rewritten before the MVP, and the comfort of a second form is a task of @MILESTONE.ADD0"
		+ "that brigade may deliver itself; a document whose code does not exist yet costs nothing"
		+ "more as entities"
		REF @MILESTONE.ADD0
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07: \"d'ailleurs: tout ce qui est un .md doit pouvoir"
		+ "être géré en utilisant awawa à la place, c'est à prévoir dans notre plan\"; on the plan"
		+ "of this decision, of @TASK.B107 and of the amendments: \"ok pour le plan ci-dessus\"; on"
		+ "the priorities: \"J'aimerais avoir une brigade opérationnelle rapidement, et"
		+ "potentiellement les améliorations non indispensables pourront être implémentée en"
		+ "utilisant brigade justement.\""
		REF @TASK.B107

DECISION TheClientIsAskedThroughOneFunctionAndTheConfigurationIsReadOncePerCommand
	TITLE "a client is asked through one function, ask_named_client, which receives the resolved"
		+ "client and the configuration; a command reads config.toml once and passes the record"
		+ "down"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the command modules that ask a client read config.toml once, through"
		+ "read_configured_client or read_optional_configuration, resolve the client through the"
		+ "runtime's resolver and pass the resolved client and the Configuration record to"
		+ "ask_named_client, which completes the question and resolves nothing"
		REF @TASK.B73
	DESC "the ask of a client goes through one function of brigade/system; the configuration"
		+ "travels from the command that read it and the system layer parses no file"
		REF @TASK.B77
	REJECTED "a second ask function, ask_configured_client, reading config.toml itself or kept as"
		+ "an alias of ask_named_client: every command already reads the configuration for the"
		+ "client's name, so it would parse the file twice, and its name no longer guaranteed that"
		+ "the client passed was the configured one"
	RATIONALE "the review of pull request #65 found the double read new in @TASK.B73 and the name"
		+ "dishonest; the draft @TASK.B77 planned to keep the function as an alias, which would"
		+ "have re-introduced it"
		REF @TASK.B73
		REF @TASK.B77
	SOURCE "the review of pull request #65, 2026-10-08, run 20261008T005404Z-e7730d"
		REF @TASK.B73

DECISION ALedgerEventDeclaresEveryFieldBrigadeWritesAndAnUnreportedMeasureIsAbsent
	TITLE "the dataclass of a ledger event declares every field brigade writes and a line must"
		+ "carry them all; a measure no collector reported is absent, never null"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a run.finished line carries the 17 fields run_segments writes and a signal.recorded line"
		+ "its 6; the reader refuses a line lacking one, as it refuses any line lacking a field of"
		+ "its event"
		REF @TASK.B74
	DESC "steps_to_first_edit and oversized_output_steps are optional on RunFinished: absent from"
		+ "the line until a collector reports them, and never written null"
	DESC "an event the ledger does not declare is read as UndeclaredEvent, its name alone: the"
		+ "overview counts it, and no wave or project view reads a key of its own"
	DESC "the answers of launch-argv and resume-argv share one shape and one kind, ClientCommand"
	REJECTED "keeping the nine fields of EVENT_FIELDS as the read contract of run.finished, the"
		+ "others optional: the dataclass would declare fields a line may lack, and the reader"
		+ "could not tell a damaged line from a complete one"
	REJECTED "writing an unreported measure null: every null of run.finished carries its reason in"
		+ "nulls, and a measure no collector exists for has none to give"
	REJECTED "skipping an undeclared event as an unreadable line: the overview counts the events of"
		+ "every name the ledger holds"
	REJECTED "one dataclass per answer of launch-argv and resume-argv: two identical declarations"
		+ "of one shape"
	REJECTED "one kind for result.json and the parse-result answer: the outcome of result.json"
		+ "admits wall_limit, the cut brigade decides when the wall limit expires, and the client"
		+ "answer never carries it; the two shapes differ, and RunResult stays a kind of its own"
	SOURCE "pull request #68 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B74"
		REF @TASK.B74

DECISION ARunKeepsAJournalOfOneShortTimestampedRecordPerActionThatTheReaderTails
	TITLE "a run keeps a journal, one short timestamped JSON record per action of its client,"
		+ "written as the run goes; brigade prints it whole and the reader takes its tail"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a run appends to runs/<id>/journal.jsonl one JSON record per action of its client,"
		+ "carrying schema_version, the time brigade read it, the segment, the kind and a summary"
		+ "of 200 characters at most, the record naming whether the summary was cut"
	DESC "the journal is written while the segment runs: the run reads the new output of the client"
		+ "every journal_poll_s seconds of config.toml, 2 by default, and once more when the"
		+ "segment ends, so that tail -f of the file follows the run"
	DESC "the actions are read by an operation actions of the client adapter, which turns the new"
		+ "output of a segment into the actions it holds; the core names no event of a client; a"
		+ "client whose adapter declares no such operation has one raw record per line of its"
		+ "stdout, cut to the same length"
	DESC "brigade runs show <id> --log prints the journal, one line per record, and --json the same"
		+ "records in a document; brigade takes no --tail and no --follow: the reader pipes the"
		+ "output into tail, or follows the file with tail -f"
	DESC "segments/<n>/stdout.log and stderr.log stay the raw output of the client, the input of"
		+ "its adapter, returned whole by no command"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B79"
		REF @TASK.B79
	REJECTED "the paths and line counts of the logs of a segment: the reader opens and searches the"
		+ "files, against DESC 2 of the decision that every trace is read through a brigade command"
	REJECTED "the raw logs returned whole or cut by --tail: the stdout of a vibe segment reached 2"
		+ "MB with a line of 200 655 characters, so a line count bounds nothing"
	REJECTED "a text journal.log followed with tail -f: a brigade reader of the journal would parse"
		+ "a rendering back"
	REJECTED "a --follow of brigade: tail already follows a file, and the reader keeps the choice"
		+ "of its bound"
	RATIONALE "the reader of a run, a person or a bot, follows what the run does, not the"
		+ "transcript of its client: vibe writes its whole session on stdout, every turn, its"
		+ "reasoning and the content of every file a tool read, and claude-code under"
		+ "--output-format json writes one result document at the end of the session"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-09 in the refinement of @TASK.B79: \"On ne devrait pas"
		+ "avoir des logs de 2mo. On devrait avoir un journal avec des entrées courtes (1"
		+ "\"ligne\") et horodatées non?\"; \"le tail n'est pas fait à l'intérieur, ça reste à moi"
		+ "(ou au bot) de passer le log en tail\"; on the format, \"en jsonl c'est bien\""
		REF @TASK.B79
